I believe this is a bug; if the level is smaller than the maximum map
area, the squares that are automatically created around it are marked
undiggable but not unphasable.  The same thing can happen in Sokoban,
and indeed even on ordinary levels if the map happens to be smaller
than the maximum size.  However, on ordinary levels it doesn't tend to
be as noticeable, since any phasing monsters generated there can just
phase into the normal area, and will usually do so (since that's where
the player is).  The one exception, besides unphaseable levels, is if
the entire normal map area is full of monsters already, as might
happen with a pudding farm or something like that.

In Sokoban, and it seems on Astral as well, however, the room walls
are unphaseable, so any xorns created or teleported "outside the
level" are stuck there.  Since both Sokoban and Astral are no-teleport
levels, there doesn't seem to be any way for the player to get there
even if polymorphed into a phasing monster.  Getting any monsters
already there out could also be difficult, although it _might_ be
possible by taming them with a scroll while confused and then using a
magic whistle.  (Does a scroll of taming work through walls?  I'm not
sure...)

Anyway, this looks like a simple oversight in the code.  I wonder if
it's been reported to the devteam, though -- I couldn't find anything
like it with a quick look at the known bugs list.

